{"id":"pacific-punk-wave","title":"Pacific Punk Wave","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Pacific_Punk_Wave","rev":238845,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Pacific Punk Wave"]}," is a visual design movement prominent from the late 1970s and 1980s that mixes Pacific ",{"t":"a","c":["New Wave"],"id":"new-wave"}," music, punk rebellion, Italian radical design and Swiss New Wave typography. It was heavily influenced by interior, post- modern graphics, and fashion trends, serving as a precursor to styles like ",{"t":"a","c":["New Wave Tropical"],"id":"new-wave-tropical"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Lite"],"id":"memphis-lite"},". It paved the way for the 1980s/1990s post-modern commercial aesthetic, inspiring digital design revivals like vector graphics and ",{"t":"a","c":["synthwave"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Synthwave"},"."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The aesthetic is defined by its usage of eye-catching and colorful patterns."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Under Construction"]}]},{"title":"Music","id":"music","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Artists / Bands"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["The Motels"]},{"c":["The B-52s"]},{"c":["Duran Duran"]},{"c":["Blondie"]},{"c":["Devo"]},{"c":["Le Tigre"]},{"c":["Madonna"]},{"c":["Crack Cloud"]},{"c":["Perturbator"]},{"c":["Empire of the Sun"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/bd/Pater_sato.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260502042622","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/2b/Goldseal_batteries.png/revision/latest?cb=20260502042604","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/64/Fantasy_20.png/revision/latest?cb=20260502042547","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/36/Inca.png/revision/latest?cb=2026050